  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.1.1: quality/audit release (rolls up the 2.1.0 window). Fixes: method-encryption no longer ships a runtime-crashing binary for members on generic instantiations/async (F-OBF-101); correct install uses the Delta1Labs.Nebula.Tool package id; opt-in verifyRun smoke-run catches crashing output a static check misses; protected crashes now embed a deobfuscate hint (symbol map + command); the baked trial time-bomb is disclosed in report.txt and --json (CI-greppable); the obfuscation report lists every applied protection; code virtualization is now a Pro feature (no longer Enterprise-gated); dependency security bumps (Microsoft.Build.Utilities.Core, Tmds.DBus.Protocol); MSBuild resolves the dotnet-tool shim explicitly; plus GUI log severity colouring, free-cap remainder signalling, deactivate-by-stored-key, and docs/exit-code/env-var corrections. Also in this window: in-app feedback/bug reporting; eval/free-only anonymous usage telemetry (buffer-first, stop-on-convert, hard-off when air-gapped); inform-only update check (never auto-installs). 1.1.5: built-in tamper telemetry (\"report-home\", tamperReportUrl) — a fired guard POSTs a minimal {\"event\":\"…\"} to your own endpoint before reacting; .NET and .NET Framework. 1.1.4: continuous environment checks (environmentChecksContinuous — AssemblyLoad hook, licensing call-site re-checks, jittered timer) and MonoMod.RuntimeDetour detection. 1.1.3: cross-platform CLI distribution (Linux/macOS/CI via dotnet tool); reference (proxy-call) obfuscation; environment & tampering-tool detection; configurable expiry guard; method-encryption anti-dump; Keyright-aware auto-protect for licensing code; metadata (#Strings heap) hardening.",
